class Solution {
    public boolean canPartition(int[] nums) {
        int sum = 0;
        for (int num : nums) {
            sum += num;
        }

        if (sum % 2 != 0) {
            return false;
        }

        int target = sum / 2;
        // memo[index][target] stores whether a target is reachable starting from index
        Boolean[][] memo = new Boolean[nums.length][target + 1];

        return dfs(0, target, nums, memo);
    }

    private boolean dfs(int i, int target, int[] nums, Boolean[][] memo) {
        if (target == 0) return true;
        if (i >= nums.length || target < 0) return false;

        // Return cached result if available
        if (memo[i][target] != null) {
            return memo[i][target];
        }

        // Compute choices and cache the result
        boolean take = dfs(i + 1, target - nums[i], nums, memo);
        boolean notTake = dfs(i + 1, target, nums, memo);

        memo[i][target] = take || notTake;
        return memo[i][target];
    }
}

//CODE END
MEMOIZED SOLUTION (TOP-DOWN DYNAMIC PROGRAMMING)
TIME COMPLEXITY: O(N * Target)

Target is defined as (Total Sum / 2).

There are N * (Target + 1) distinct subproblem states represented by the pair (index, target).

Each state is calculated at most once. Subsequent calls with the same (index, target) return instantly from the memo table in O(1) time.

SPACE COMPLEXITY: O(N * Target)

Memoization table space: The memo array of size N x (Target + 1) takes O(N * Target) space in memory.

Auxiliary call stack space: O(N) space reserved for the recursive function call stack depth.

Total space complexity: O(N * Target) + O(N) = O(N * Target).
